{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Only to the parokhet, and to the altar.</b> If it said 'to the parokhet' but did not say 'and to the altar,' I would say: to the parokhet, which is inside, he is disqualified, but to the altar, which is not inside, he is not disqualified — therefore 'and to the altar' is stated. And if it said 'and to the altar' but did not say 'to the parokhet,' I would say: and to the altar, which is fit for service, he shall be disqualified, but to the parokhet, which is not fit for service, he shall not be disqualified — therefore it must say 'to the parokhet and to the altar.'" "<b>For I am HaShem who sanctifies them.</b> The parokhet and the altar, and no blemished man is fit to come to them."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:10.892527973Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}